  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/206) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello Alberto, I think I’ve found a little problem with the brush mask, it seems that I can’t leave the tool. \n\nOpen a raw, go to Local Editing, activate Color/Tone Correction, then activate the brush mask. Paint a mask, the cursor has changed to a circle. Switch off the Brush mask, the circle is still visible. Switch Brush mask on again, go to the first tab, activate the Exposure tool, or whatever. Paint again on the photo and we’re still creating a mask! \n\nThe point is that it seems that I can’t leave the tool. The tooltip says Use the **third** button to switch off the paint tool, but my mouse only has two buttons and a scroll wheel. My Wacom pen that I use by default only has a left and a right button and Ctrl\\+second button \\(the right one?\\) does nothing. Clicking the Hand tool on top of the editor doesn’t change anything either. \n\nI noticed this week for the first time that right clicking on the photo toggles the two sliders for radius and strength. Perhaps this ‘lock-in’ comes from here? \n\nOn Linux, latest Art code from git, home compiled.\n\nRegards, Paul.\n",
